<section class="container sec" id="takeaways" aria-label="Key takeaways">
  <h2 class="part-head">Key takeaways</h2>
  <aside class="takeaways" aria-label="Key takeaways">
    <ul>
      <li><span><b>Motion is the bottleneck.</b> Every model recovers appearance and geometry far better than how the scene moves, the strongest included.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Agents describe motion instead of simulating it.</b> Most solutions write motion as hand-tuned curves and few build a simulation: models do not yet truly understand physics.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>More reasoning, more simulation.</b> <span class="mref"><img class="mono" src="logos/gpt.svg" alt="">GPT-6 Astra</span> leads the Pareto frontier, and as its reasoning effort rises, it simulates more often and reconstructs motion better.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Real-world footage remains the hard case.</b> Models that reconstruct simulated scenes well fall short on real videos.</span></li>
      <li><span><b>Open-weight models still lag.</b> Even the best open-weight model trails the leading proprietary ones by a wide margin.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </aside>
</section>

